Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• TRANSACTIONS  
  – "from_address" / "to_address": identify sender / receiver of a normal ETH‑transfer transaction  
  – "value": Wei amount transferred (used for balance, avg in/out amounts, …)  
  – "gas_price", "receipt_gas_used": compute paid fees (gas_price × receipt_gas_used)  
  – "receipt_status": keep only successful transactions (=1)  
  – "block_timestamp", "block_number": filter to activity before 2017‑01‑01 & create time based metrics  
  – "hash": transaction identifier (join helper)  

• TRACES  
  – "from_address" / "to_address": sender / receiver for internal transactions  
  – "trace_type": differentiate between call, create, reward, …  
  – "call_type": exclude "delegatecall", "callcode", "staticcall" when needed  
  – "value": Wei transferred internally  
  – "gas_used": measure gas for incoming “call” traces  
  – "status": success / failure flag  
  – "block_timestamp", "block_number": same temporal filters  

• TOKEN_TRANSFERS  
  – "from_address" / "to_address": token senders & receivers  
  – "token_address": which ERC‑20 was moved (count types)  
  – "value": amount of tokens moved  
  – "block_timestamp", "block_number": time filters  

• CONTRACTS  
  – "address": the deployed contract address (creator derived from TRACES where trace_type='create')  
  – "bytecode": length => contract bytecode size  
  – "block_timestamp": deployment time  

• BLOCKS  
  – not used directly for most metrics; mining rewards are already available in TRACES where trace_type='reward'  

• TOKENS  
  – look up token metadata (name / symbol / decimals) if needed for token type counts  

Main conditions often used  
• "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000    -- before 2017‑01‑01 (micro‑seconds)  
• "receipt_status" = 1 (TRANSACTIONS) or "status" = 1 (TRACES)  
• Exclude TRACES where "call_type" IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall')  


------------------------------------------------------------------------  
Example exploration queries (Snowflake SQL) – each limited to 20 rows  

```sql
-- 1) Description: Distinct externally‑owned addresses that sent a transaction before 2017‑01‑01
SELECT DISTINCT "from_address" AS "address"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRANSACTIONS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Sample incoming ETH transfers (internal ‘call’ traces) to any address before 2017
SELECT "to_address",
       "value",
       "block_number",
       "block_timestamp"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRACES"
WHERE "trace_type" = 'call'
  AND "status" = 1
  AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND ( "call_type" IS NULL
        OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall') )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Sample contract‑creation traces before 2017 (creator in "from_address")
SELECT "from_address"        AS "creator",
       "to_address"          AS "contract_address",
       "value",
       "block_number"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRACES"
WHERE "trace_type" = 'create'
  AND "status" = 1
  AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Mining reward traces before 2017 – who received the reward and how much (Wei)
SELECT "to_address"   AS "miner",
       SUM("value")   AS "total_reward_wei"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRACES"
WHERE "trace_type" = 'reward'
  AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
GROUP BY "to_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Token transfers received by an address (example) before 2017
SELECT "to_address",
       "token_address",
       "value",
       "block_number"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TOKEN_TRANSFERS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "to_address" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Count of distinct token types sent by each address before 2017
SELECT "from_address",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "token_address") AS "token_out_type"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TOKEN_TRANSFERS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
GROUP BY "from_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Average & stddev of gas used for successful incoming call traces per receiver
SELECT "to_address",
       AVG("gas_used") AS "avg_gas_used",
       STDDEV("gas_used") AS "std_gas_used"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRACES"
WHERE "trace_type" = 'call'
  AND "status" = 1
  AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND ( "call_type" IS NULL
        OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall') )
GROUP BY "to_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Failed outgoing transactions count by address (receipt_status = 0)
SELECT "from_address",
       COUNT(*) AS "failure_count"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRANSACTIONS"
WHERE "receipt_status" = 0
  AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
GROUP BY "from_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Bytecode size for contracts created before 2017
SELECT "address"         AS "contract_address",
       LENGTH("bytecode") AS "bytecode_size"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."CONTRACTS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Comprehensive preview – incoming vs outgoing normal transfers (ETH) for each address
SELECT adr,
       SUM(CASE WHEN dir = 'in'  THEN val_eth ELSE 0 END) AS "eth_in",
       SUM(CASE WHEN dir = 'out' THEN val_eth ELSE 0 END) AS "eth_out",
       COUNT_IF(dir = 'in')  AS "in_tnx",
       COUNT_IF(dir = 'out') AS "out_tnx"
FROM (
    SELECT "to_address"   AS adr,
           'in'           AS dir,
           "value"/1e18   AS val_eth
    FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRANSACTIONS"
    WHERE "receipt_status" = 1
      AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
      AND "to_address" IS NOT NULL
    UNION ALL
    SELECT "from_address" AS adr,
           'out'          AS dir,
           "value"/1e18   AS val_eth
    FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN."TRANSACTIONS"
    WHERE "receipt_status" = 1
      AND "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
      AND "from_address" IS NOT NULL
) t
GROUP BY adr
LIMIT 20;
```

These sample queries illustrate how to explore and aggregate the key metrics required for the full address‑level report while adhering to the specified schema, quoting conventions, and time filters.
